---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';

const questions = [
  { move: 'Open', qs: ['What’s something at work you do regularly that costs more than it should?'], stuck: ['What did you redo this week?', 'What were you waiting on last week, and on whom?', 'What do you put off until the deadline forces it?'] },
  { move: 'Anchor', qs: ['When did you last do it?', 'What kicked it off?', 'How did it end?'] },
  { move: 'Goal, provisional', qs: ['When that was finished, what existed that didn’t exist before?'], stuck: ['An activity is named: what was that for?', 'Too large: what did you do on Thursday?'] },
  { move: 'Dump', qs: ['Everything that happened between the kick-off and the end. Past tense, one thing per line, any order.', 'What else?', 'What did you wait for?', 'Who did you have to remind?', 'What went wrong?'] },
  { move: 'Order', qs: ['Put those in the order they happened.', 'Where are the natural breaks?', 'What would you call each part?'] },
  { move: 'Operations', per: 'per part', qs: ['What did you physically do here: open, write, send, check?', 'How many drafts?', 'What would a stranger get wrong doing this?'] },
  { move: 'Inputs and outputs', per: 'per operation', qs: ['What did you need to start this?', 'Where did it come from?', 'What did it produce?', 'Who got it?'] },
  { move: 'Allocation', per: 'per operation', qs: ['Where on this ladder does this one sit today?'], stuck: ['Rung 0–2: why do you stay in?', 'None of the four reasons: does it go up one?', 'Kept: is it the gathering, the thinking, the deciding, or the doing you want to keep?'] },
  { move: 'Goal, revised', qs: ['You kept these. Why do they matter?', 'And why does that matter? Until the answer stops changing.', 'Say that without naming a tool or a step.', 'Suppose the built parts are running and the kept parts are yours. What’s the first thing you notice on a Monday?'] },
  { move: 'Close', qs: ['What did you notice today that you hadn’t seen before?'] },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="The agent — Make It So Camp Tokyo"
  description="The Make It So agent: an interview that takes one piece of your work and writes it down well enough to hand to a machine."
  canonicalPath="/new/tokyo/agent/"
  robots="noindex, nofollow"
>
  <Header links={[
    { label: 'What it is', href: '#what' },
    { label: 'The conversation', href: '#flow' },
    { label: 'The questions', href: '#questions' },
    { label: 'Where it stands', href: '#status' },
    { label: 'The camp', href: '/new/tokyo/' },
  ]} />

  <Hero
    leftMeta="The agent"
    rightMeta={'Make It So Camp Tokyo<br><span class="light">in development</span>'}
    statement="One piece of your work, written down well enough to hand to a machine."
    small={true}
    minHeight="42svh"
  />

  <section class="section" id="what" aria-labelledby="what-label">
    <div class="section-label"><span class="num">01</span><h2 class="label" id="what-label">What it is</h2></div>
    <p class="lead-statement">An interview, run by an agent. <span class="dim">Not a form.</span></p>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <p>People cannot describe their own work in the abstract. Asked for a workflow, they draw three boxes or forty, and both are fiction. The time goes into waiting, chasing, rework and exceptions, and none of that appears in a self-report. What people can describe is last Tuesday.</p>
        <p>So the agent asks about last Tuesday. It takes one thing you do regularly, finds the last time you did it, and walks down from the goal to the parts to the steps, one question at a time. Then it asks, step by step, how much of it you want to keep doing yourself.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p><strong>What you leave with.</strong> A card: the goal, the steps, what each step needs and produces, which steps stay with you and why, and which ones get built. The card is in your words. It is the written-down method, and it is what any agent can be handed afterwards.</p>
        <p><strong>The turn.</strong> The goal is asked twice. Once at the start, stated from inside the work as it is now. Once at the end, worked upward from the steps you refused to hand off. If the two differ, the difference is the result.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="flow" aria-labelledby="flow-label">
    <div class="section-label"><span class="num">02</span><h2 class="label" id="flow-label">The conversation</h2></div>
    <p class="lead-statement">The work, taken apart.</p>
    <figure class="flow">
<svg viewBox="0 0 1200 620" role="img" aria-label="One piece of work decomposed: a goal at the top, three subgoals under it, activities under each, every activity with a rung from 0 to 4 and, for rungs 0 to 2, a reason. Activities at rung 0 to 1 stay with the person and feed a revised goal beside the first. Activities at rung 2 to 4 get built, one per session, and after a real run the tree is redrawn. Everything lands on the card. Rails name steps 1 to 3 of the camp's list.">
<defs>
<marker id="arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="currentColor"/></marker>
<marker id="arrA" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="var(--accent)"/></marker>
</defs>
<g font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="13">
<!-- rails -->
<g fill="var(--muted)" font-size="11" letter-spacing="1.4">
<text x="20" y="112">1 · THINK OF IT</text><text x="20" y="126">AS A WORKFLOW</text>
<text x="20" y="262">2 · INPUTS AND</text><text x="20" y="276">OUTPUTS, PER</text><text x="20" y="290">ACTIVITY</text>
<text x="720" y="196">3 · DECIDE WHERE A PERSON STAYS IN</text>
</g>
<g stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1"><line x1="150" y1="40" x2="150" y2="190"/><line x1="150" y1="212" x2="150" y2="360"/></g>
<!-- goal 1 -->
<rect x="180" y="40" width="480" height="56" rx="2" fill="var(--bg)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
<text x="196" y="60" font-size="11" fill="var(--muted)" letter-spacing="1.4">GOAL, AS STATED</text>
<text x="196" y="82" fill="currentColor">The board trusts the numbers without me re-explaining them every month</text>
<!-- goal 2 -->
<rect x="720" y="40" width="460" height="56" rx="2" fill="#F2E9E4" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.6"/>
<text x="736" y="60" font-size="11" fill="var(--accent)" letter-spacing="1.4">GOAL, REVISED</text>
<text x="736" y="82" fill="currentColor">A board that gets a trustworthy number without me explaining it live</text>
<text x="690" y="64" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="11">same, or</text>
<text x="690" y="78" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="11">different?</text>
<!-- goal -> subgoals -->
<line x1="420" y1="97" x2="420" y2="118" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<line x1="255" y1="118" x2="585" y2="118" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#arr)"><line x1="255" y1="118" x2="255" y2="138"/><line x1="420" y1="118" x2="420" y2="138"/><line x1="585" y1="118" x2="585" y2="138"/></g>
<!-- subgoals -->
<g stroke="currentColor" fill="var(--bg)" stroke-width="1.2"><rect x="180" y="140" width="150" height="44" rx="2"/><rect x="345" y="140" width="150" height="44" rx="2"/><rect x="510" y="140" width="150" height="44" rx="2"/></g>
<g fill="currentColor" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle"><text x="255" y="159">Pull the metrics</text><text x="420" y="159">Write the narrative</text><text x="585" y="159">Build and send</text></g>
<g fill="var(--muted)" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle"><text x="255" y="175">subgoal</text><text x="420" y="175">subgoal</text><text x="585" y="175">subgoal</text></g>
<g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#arr)"><line x1="255" y1="185" x2="255" y2="218"/><line x1="420" y1="185" x2="420" y2="218"/><line x1="585" y1="185" x2="585" y2="218"/></g>
<!-- activities -->
<g stroke="currentColor" fill="var(--bg)" stroke-width="1">
<rect x="180" y="220" width="150" height="40" rx="2"/><rect x="180" y="268" width="150" height="40" rx="2"/><rect x="180" y="316" width="150" height="40" rx="2"/>
<rect x="345" y="220" width="150" height="40" rx="2"/><rect x="345" y="268" width="150" height="40" rx="2"/>
<rect x="510" y="220" width="150" height="40" rx="2"/><rect x="510" y="268" width="150" height="40" rx="2"/><rect x="510" y="316" width="150" height="40" rx="2"/>
</g>
<g fill="currentColor" font-size="12">
<text x="190" y="236">Export MRR and churn</text><text x="190" y="284">Reconcile against ledger</text><text x="190" y="332">One line per metric</text>
<text x="355" y="236">Draft the headline story</text><text x="355" y="284">Edit down to one page</text>
<text x="520" y="236">Lay out the slides</text><text x="520" y="284">Build the charts</text><text x="520" y="332">Answer the follow-ups</text>
</g>
<g font-size="11">
<text x="190" y="252" fill="var(--muted)">rung 3 · spot-check</text>
<text x="190" y="300" fill="var(--accent)">● rung 1 · judgment</text>
<text x="190" y="348" fill="var(--accent)">● rung 0 · judgment</text>
<text x="355" y="252" fill="var(--accent)">● rung 1 · judgment</text>
<text x="355" y="300" fill="var(--muted)">rung 2 · consequence</text>
<text x="520" y="252" fill="var(--muted)">rung 4 · never see it</text>
<text x="520" y="300" fill="var(--muted)">rung 3 · spot-check</text>
<text x="520" y="348" fill="var(--accent)">● rung 0 · relationship</text>
</g>
<!-- right column -->
<rect x="720" y="212" width="460" height="64" rx="2" fill="#F2E9E4" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<text x="736" y="234" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor">● Stays with you</text>
<text x="736" y="252" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">rung 0–1, each with a reason: consequence, judgment,</text>
<text x="736" y="266" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">relationship, or learning. Habit does not count.</text>
<rect x="720" y="300" width="460" height="64" rx="2" fill="var(--bg)" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<text x="736" y="322" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor">Gets built</text>
<text x="736" y="340" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">rung 2–4. One activity per session; you say how you'd know</text>
<text x="736" y="354" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">the result is good before anything is built.</text>
<!-- tree -> right -->
<path d="M661,240 L690,240 L690,244 L718,244" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrA)"/>
<path d="M661,336 L690,336 L690,332 L718,332" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
<!-- stays -> goal 2 -->
<path d="M950,211 L950,98" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.4" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrA)"/>
<text x="960" y="130" fill="var(--accent)" font-size="11">“why does this matter?”</text>
<text x="960" y="144" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="11">and again, until the answer stops changing</text>
<text x="960" y="158" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="11">then restated with no tool or step named</text>
<!-- redraw -->
<path d="M950,365 L950,400 L420,400 L420,318" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="5 4" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrA)"/>
<text x="700" y="418" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--accent)" font-size="11" letter-spacing="1.2">AFTER ONE REAL RUN · REDRAW THE TREE</text>
<text x="700" y="432" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="11">automating an activity changes the work around it: new checking, new chasing</text>
<!-- card -->
<line x1="255" y1="357" x2="255" y2="470" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
<rect x="180" y="472" width="1000" height="60" rx="2" fill="#E3DED3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"/>
<text x="196" y="494" font-size="11" fill="var(--muted)" letter-spacing="1.4">THE CARD</text>
<text x="196" y="514" fill="currentColor">Goal · subgoals · activities with what each needs and produces · a rung and a reason per activity · what stays, what gets built · the revised goal. In your words.</text>
<text x="196" y="560" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="12">Steps 4 to 8 on the list, from writing the brief to sharing what you built, read from the card. Step 9 is the dashed loop.</text>
<text x="196" y="590" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="11">Example workflow: a monthly investor update. Invented for illustration.</text>
</g>
</svg>

      <figcaption>One piece of work, taken apart: the goal, three subgoals, the activities under them, and a rung for every activity. What the person keeps feeds the revised goal; what gets built comes back to redraw the tree. All of it lands on the card.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="questions" aria-labelledby="questions-label">
    <div class="section-label"><span class="num">03</span><h2 class="label" id="questions-label">The questions</h2></div>
    <p class="lead-statement">Fixed wording. <span class="dim">A paraphrase drifts toward “how do you usually”, and the answer to that is fiction.</span></p>
    <div class="day-list qlist">
      {questions.map((q) => (
        <div class="day-row">
          <div class="day-label"><strong>{q.move}</strong>{q.per && <span class="light"><br>{q.per}</span>}</div>
          <div>
            <ul>
              {q.qs.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
              {q.stuck && q.stuck.map((s) => <li class="stuck">{s}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="keep" aria-labelledby="keep-label">
    <div class="section-label"><span class="num">04</span><h2 class="label" id="keep-label">How much stays with you</h2></div>
    <p class="lead-statement">A ladder, and four reasons to stay on it.</p>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <p>Each step gets a rung. Replace-me-entirely or leave-it-alone is the wrong question; most steps sit in between, and the interesting ones sit at different rungs for the gathering, the thinking, the deciding and the doing.</p>
        <dl class="facts ladder">
          <dt>0</dt><dd>I do it</dd>
          <dt>1</dt><dd>It drafts, I finish</dd>
          <dt>2</dt><dd>It does, I approve every one</dd>
          <dt>3</dt><dd>It does, I spot-check the batch</dd>
          <dt>4</dt><dd>It does, I never see it</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Anything at rung 0 to 2 needs a reason, and only four count. <strong>Consequence:</strong> it goes outside and is hard to reverse. <strong>Judgment:</strong> there is no ground truth, only taste. <strong>Relationship:</strong> someone needs to know a person did it. <strong>Learning:</strong> it is where your signal comes from.</p>
        <p>Habit is not on the list. If none of the four applies, the step goes up a rung. What someone refuses to hand off says what they think the work is for, better than anything they said at the start; that is why the goal is asked again at the end, from those steps.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="status" aria-labelledby="status-label">
    <div class="section-label"><span class="num">05</span><h2 class="label" id="status-label">Where it stands</h2></div>
    <p class="lead-statement">Two front ends, one interview. <span class="dim">Neither is finished.</span></p>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <p><strong>As a skill.</strong> A Claude Code skill that runs the interview in text, writes the card to disk, and then builds one step from it with whatever the machine has, against a pass condition the participant wrote before anything was built. Built by Noah, with the interview design from Tokyo folded in.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p><strong>As a live card.</strong> A prototype connector for Claude that runs the same interview with the card filling in on screen, the ladder as something you tap, and the two goals side by side at the end. The server refuses to move on before a step’s exit condition is met. Built by Igor; runs locally, not yet deployed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <p>Neither has been run on a real participant. Both share the questions above and produce the same card, so whichever front end holds up in a real room carries the other one with it.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@misocamp.com">hello@misocamp.com</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .flow { margin:clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 3rem) 0 0; padding:clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem); border:1px solid var(--line); overflow-x:auto; color:var(--ink); }
  .flow svg { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; min-width:900px; }
  .flow figcaption { margin-top:1rem; max-width:70ch; color:var(--muted); font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.5; }
  .qlist { margin-top:clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 3rem); }
  .qlist ul { margin:0; padding-left:1.1rem; max-width:60ch; }
  .qlist li { margin:0.25rem 0; font-size:clamp(1rem, 1.1vw, 1.12rem); line-height:1.5; }
  .qlist li.stuck { color:var(--muted); }
  .ladder { margin-top:1.2rem; }
  .ladder dt { font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
</style>
